# <type>(<scope>): <subject, imperative, under 72 chars, no trailing period>
#
# - <body bullet: only if it says something the subject doesn't>
# - <3 bullets max, one line each. No body at all is often correct.>
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enable this template once per clone:
#
#     git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# type   feat  fix  docs  chore  refactor  test  build  perf  ci  style
#
# scope  net  hud  render  physics  weapons  audio  cmake  ci  lint
#        docs  tests
#
# Rules (see CLAUDE.md section 3):
#   - Subject under 72 chars, imperative mood: "add", not "added".
#   - Body: 3 bullets max. No prose paragraphs.
#   - Don't re-list the files you touched — the diff already did.
#   - If it needs a long explanation, that explanation is an ADR.
#     Write the ADR and cite it: "See ADR-006."
#
# Good:
#   fix(net): clamp rewind window to 200 ms
#
#   - Anti-cheat: fake high ping was buying a wider rewind. See ADR-006.
#
# Bad:
#   Updated a bunch of netcode files and also fixed the docs and the CI
#   because the rewind was wrong and I noticed some other things too
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
